(Only "none" with exactly "move" or "bind" is the pattern; anything close to it is mounted as given.)
(The target does not exist, so the kernel refuses with ENOENT whatever the caller's privileges.)
a text called kind is "none".
a text called 'almost none' is "non".
a text called 'empty type' is "".
a text called 'none and more' is "nonetheless".
a buffer called 'blank options' is 16 bytes.
a text called 'almost bind' is "bin".
a text called binder is "binder".
a text called moved is "moved".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_755_no_such_target" with type 'almost none' with options "bind".
On error print "a type of non stayed a plain mount".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_755_no_such_target" with type 'none and more' with options "move".
On error print "a type of nonetheless stayed a plain mount".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_755_no_such_target" with type 'empty type' with options "bind".
On error print "an empty type stayed a plain mount".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_755_no_such_target" with type kind with options 'almost bind'.
On error print "options of bin stayed a plain mount".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_755_no_such_target" with type kind with options binder.
On error print "options of binder stayed a plain mount".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_755_no_such_target" with type kind with options moved.
On error print "options of moved stayed a plain mount".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_755_no_such_target" with type kind with options 'blank options'.
On error print "empty options stayed a plain mount".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_755_no_such_target" with type "tmpfs" with options binder.
On error print "a literal tmpfs type stayed a plain mount".
